  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "Follow just one photosite on the sensor. Light enters it and becomes an electrical signal. More light makes a larger signal. But that signal is only a brightness measurement. This site's filter passes mostly green light. So it records green brightness at this location. Neighbouring sites record red or blue through their filters. The processor compares neighbours to estimate each site's missing color values. This step is called Demosaicing. Now red, green and blue values describe one colored pixel. Repeat that millions of times, then reduce noise and adjust brightness. Many tiny measurements become the photograph you see.",
